+## 9. No Default to Unidentified
+
+**Added 2026-09-04. Equal authority to the Five Laws.**
+
+"Joan — unidentified" is not a resting state. It is only an acceptable *current* status for a model once that model's plausible remote-accessible record types (per its row in `research_queue/HYPOTHESIS_TEST_MATRIX.md`) have actually been searched — not merely reasoned about.
+
+- A model does not get marked "exhausted" because it seems less likely than another — see Law 3. It gets marked exhausted because its specific record types were searched and returned nothing.
+- The goal is not to confirm Model A, or any single model. The goal is Joan's actual mother, father, siblings, and life — by whichever model the evidence supports. Models are a search structure, not a scoreboard.
+- The same standard applies by proxy to every John Greene in the John Firewall (`theory/john_firewall.md`): no John's status stays at 🟡 or ⚪ by default when a free, remote-accessible source could move it to 🟢 or 🔴. If a John's status hasn't changed, that means the source hasn't been checked yet — not that it can't be found.
+- This project has no institutional access and does no in-person archive travel (see `PROJECT_METHODOLOGY.md`). That constraint changes *how* a record type gets checked — free full-text search first, then a remote scan/microfilm request — never *whether* it gets checked.
+
+---
+
